// A note spend: the prover shows knowledge of the secret key that owns a note and
// publishes the note's nullifier, without revealing the key. The nullifier is the key
// and the note position absorbed through the permutation; it is deterministic, so the
// same note yields the same nullifier and a double spend is caught, yet it leaks
// nothing about the key. The spend authority is the ability to produce it at all.
// Run: zkolang shield/spend.zkl
include "hash.zkl";

secret sk;
input position;

// The nullifier that marks this note spent.
output permute(sk + position);
